        "long_desc": "Contributed asset development and systems design to a collaborative educational game exploring substance dependency. Proposed the Kowloon-inspired megastructure setting; dense, vertical, claustrophobic architecture mirroring addiction's psychological trap. Modeled environmental pieces and alien humanoid characters in Blender, textured in Photoshop, integrated into Unity. Co-designed mechanic-as-metaphor systems where \"drugs\" function as ability modifiers with compounding consequences: speed boosts followed by slower-than-baseline crashes, anxiety relief with escalating side effects. Worked with three teammates on concept documentation and C# implementation. Used alien protagonists for educational distance; acknowledging we weren't addiction professionals. Project remained in pre-production due to institutional disruption (campus strike, scheduling conflicts). Demonstrates 3D modeling, texturing workflows, game systems design, and collaborative development.",
        "long_mept": "",
        "long_outcome": "",
        "format": "Video Game",
        "tags": "Games × Education",

        "featured": "No",

        "collaboration": "Team",
