        "thumbnail_alt": "Prototype of nails being 3D printed",

        "affiliation": "Art/MAS, Wellesley College",
        "date": "Feb – Apr 2025",
        "end_year": "2025",
        "short_desc": "Custom-fit nails, designed and printed from a scan of your own fingers.\n<div class=\"front-outcome card-summary\">&#x2514; Wearable prototype (replicable system)</div>",
        "key_skills": ["3D Modeling", "Product Design", "Traditional Media"],

        "med_desc": "Designed a personalized press-on nail system using 3D scanning and parametric modeling — making custom fit accessible beyond mass production's one-size-fits-all standard.",
        "method_concept": "Method",
        "key_tools": ["3D Scanner", "Blender", "3D Printer"],
        "short_mept": ["1. 3D scanning nail geometry & contours", "2. Parametric modeling of custom-fit bases", "3. Iterative prototyping & curvature refinement", "4. Printing & hand-painted embellishment"],
        "short_outcome": ["Wearable prototype", "Replicable system"],

        "role": "Designer & Sculptor",
        "all_tools": ["3D Scanner", "Blender", "3D Printer", "PLA", "Gel Polish"],
        "all_skills": ["3D Modeling", "Product Design", "Traditional Media"],
        "modal_files": ["./assets/custom-nails/nails_capture_one.png", "./assets/custom-nails/nails_capture_two.png", "./assets/custom-nails/nails_prototype_one.png", "./assets/custom-nails/nails_prototype_two.png", "./assets/custom-nails/nails_embellish_one.png", "./assets/custom-nails/nails_embellish_two.png"],
        "modal_files_alt": ["Initial 3D scan of my hand", "Rendered scan ready for printing and for modelling", "Prototype of nails being 3D printed", "First prototype of nails being 3D printed", "Initial fit check with prototype nails", "Filed, polished, and designed nails - Ombre set", "Filed, polished, and designed nails - WOAW UAW! set (Workers Unions)"],
        "long_desc": "Press-on nails are designed for a standardized nail shape that doesn't exist - they fit poorly, feel uncomfortable, and pop off constantly. I 3D scanned my own fingers to capture exact nail geometry and surrounding contours, then used Blender to model custom-fit bases. After iterative prototyping to refine curvature and adhesion surface area, I 3D printed the final pieces and added hand-painted embellishments. The result: press-on nails that actually fit. This project bridges digital fabrication and traditional craft: using scanning and parametric modeling to solve a fit problem that mass production ignores. Read more about it in the featured section below.",
